<%--
Impersonation_Banner - the strip that says this session is signed in AS someone else.

Renders nothing unless the framework's window.rsxapp.impersonation block is set (a staff
session between Session::begin_impersonation() and stop_impersonation()). Read at render,
and every impersonation begin or stop is a full page load, so there is nothing to watch.

It names the effective user (window.rsxapp.user, already the impersonated membership) and
the real principal behind the session (impersonator_email), and links "Stop impersonating"
to the system panel's stop route - the one way this application begins an impersonation
is the panel's "Sign in as this user", and that route hands the developer back their own
identity and site and lands on the user they were viewing. The link is a STRING route
target (Rsx.Route('_Sys_Impersonation_Controller::stop')), published into every bundle by
the framework; an application that adds its own staff impersonation links its own stop
here instead.

No arguments.

    <Impersonation_Banner />
--%>
<Define:Impersonation_Banner tag="div">
    <% const _imp = window.rsxapp.impersonation; %>
    <% if (_imp) { %>
        <div class="Impersonation_Banner__bar" role="status">
            <i class="bi bi-incognito Impersonation_Banner__icon"></i>
            <span class="Impersonation_Banner__text">
                Signed in as <strong><%= window.rsxapp.user ? window.rsxapp.user.email : 'another user' %></strong>
                by <strong><%= _imp.impersonator_email || ('login #' + _imp.impersonator_login_user_id) %></strong>
            </span>
            <a class="Impersonation_Banner__stop" href="<%= Rsx.Route('_Sys_Impersonation_Controller::stop') %>">
                <i class="bi bi-box-arrow-left"></i> Stop impersonating
            </a>
        </div>
    <% } %>
</Define:Impersonation_Banner>
